<title>UK: TABLE-Allied Carpets yr profits up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Allied Carpets yr profits up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 12.7		  vs  10.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   5.0		  vs   nil</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)   7.5		  vs   nil</p>
<p> Pretax			16.7		  vs  14.6</p>
<p> Turnover		   255.7		  vs 230.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name - Allied Carpets Plc</p>
<p>Chairman Julian Lee said in a statement: &quot;I am pleased to be able to report that there has been a marked return to consumer confidence following a temporary drop in demand during the general election. Over the last six weeks since mid-June like for like sales growth has been 14 percent and I look forward to reporting further progress in the current year&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
